course: dictionary
lesson: 15881
title: Uninjured: not hurt
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word uninjured is made of two parts. The prefix un- means not, and injured means hurt or harmed. Put them together and uninjured means not hurt at all. When you meet a long word, look for a prefix at the start and a root word you already know.
explain: «All the passengers were uninjured» after the bus crash. The news is saying nobody was hurt. «The driver escaped uninjured» tells you the driver got away from danger with no hurt at all. Always ask: does the sentence still make sense if I put in not hurt? If it does, you have the right meaning.
explain: Uninjured is about the body. «Uninjured but shaken» shows that a person can have no cuts or bruises and still feel frightened or upset. Shaken is about feelings, but uninjured is about harm to the body. Watch for the phrases escape uninjured and walk away uninjured, which both mean getting out of danger without being hurt.
fact: Uninjured is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as passengers or driver.
fact: «Uninjured» means not hurt or harmed; without any injury.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so «unhurt» and «uninjured» have similar meanings.
fact: «Escape uninjured» means get away from danger without being hurt.
fact: The opposite of uninjured is injured, as in «The driver was injured» means the driver was hurt.
exercise: «All the passengers were uninjured after the crash.» What does uninjured mean? | Lost their bags | Still asleep | *Not hurt | Very angry
exercise: «The driver escaped uninjured.» Which word has the same meaning as uninjured? | *Unhurt | Injured | Trapped | Frightened
exercise: Mia says, «The cat walked away uninjured, but it was shaken.» What does uninjured tell us about the cat? | *Its body was not hurt | It was badly hurt | It was lost forever | It was hungry
test: What does the prefix un- mean in uninjured? | Very | Again | Under | *Not
test: «The children walked away uninjured but shaken.» Which is true? | They were badly hurt | They felt happy and calm | They were not in the crash at all | *Their bodies were not hurt, but they felt upset
exam: Which sentence uses uninjured correctly? | She was uninjured, so she needed a doctor for her broken leg | The uninjured bus was on fire | The boy was uninjured, and his arm was broken | *After the fall, the boy stood up uninjured, without a scratch on him
